# Operations

## Deploy
{% if values.enableCICD %}
The `Deploy` workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) runs on pull requests
(plan only) and on `main` (plan, then apply). It does nothing until these
repository settings exist (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):

| Name | Kind | Value |
| ---- | ---- | ----- |
| `AWS_ROLE_ARN` | Secret or variable | IAM role the workflow assumes through GitHub's OIDC provider |
| `TF_STATE_BUCKET` | Variable | S3 bucket that stores the Terraform state |
| `TF_STATE_REGION` | Variable, optional | Region of that bucket when it is not `${{ values.awsRegion or 'us-east-1' }}` |

The role must trust `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` for this repository
and be allowed to manage API Gateway, Lambda, IAM roles, CloudWatch,
DynamoDB, WAF and Cognito resources, and to read and write the state bucket.
The apply job uses the GitHub environment `production`; add required
reviewers to it to approve deployments.

After a successful apply the job summary shows the API URL.
{% else %}
No deployment workflow was requested for this repository. Deploy from a
workstation or your own pipeline as described below.
{% endif %}
### From a workstation

```bash
# 1. Build the deployment package (see Development)
# 2. Deploy
cd infra
terraform init \
  -backend-config="bucket=<state bucket>" \
  -backend-config="key=${{ values.destination.repo }}/terraform.tfstate" \
  -backend-config="region=${{ values.awsRegion or 'us-east-1' }}" \
  -backend-config="use_lockfile=true"
terraform apply
terraform output api_url
```

## Change the configuration

The choices made when the repository was created are in
`infra/terraform.tfvars.json`. Every one of them is a Terraform variable
described in `infra/variables.tf`; change the value, open a pull request and
read the plan.

| Variable | Effect |
| -------- | ------ |
| `enable_auth`, `auth_type` | `jwt`, `apikey`, `cognito` or `none` |
| `jwt_issuer`, `jwt_audience`, `jwt_jwks_uri` | Tokens the authorizer accepts (`auth_type` `jwt`; needs the `authorizer/` directory of a repository created with JWT authentication) |
| `enable_waf` | WAF web ACL in front of the stage |
| `enable_rate_limiting`, `requests_per_second` | Throttling of the stage, the usage plan and the WAF rate rule |
| `lambda_runtime`, `lambda_memory_size`, `lambda_timeout` | Function settings |
| `enable_crud` | The `/items` endpoints and their DynamoDB table |
| `endpoints` | Additional routes sent to the function |
| `enable_monitoring`, `enable_xray`, `log_retention_days` | Logs, metrics, alarms, dashboard, tracing |
| `alarm_topic_arn` | SNS topic that receives alarm notifications |
| `manage_account_logging_role` | Whether this configuration sets the account's API Gateway logging role |

The stage is named after the major version in `api_version`. Changing the
major version replaces the stage and therefore the URL.

## Monitor
{% if values.enableMonitoring %}
- Dashboard `${{ values.apiName }}` in CloudWatch: requests, errors, latency,
  function invocations and duration.
- Alarms: `${{ values.apiName }}-api-5xx`, `${{ values.apiName }}-api-latency`,
  `${{ values.apiName }}-lambda-errors`, `${{ values.apiName }}-lambda-throttles`. They are visible in
  CloudWatch; set `alarm_topic_arn` to be notified.
- Access logs: log group `/aws/apigateway/${{ values.apiName }}/access`.
- Function logs: log group `/aws/lambda/${{ values.apiName }}`.

API Gateway writes logs with one IAM role per account and region. This
configuration creates that role and sets it in the account settings. If the
account already has one, set `manage_account_logging_role` to `false`.
{% else %}
Detailed monitoring was not requested. Function logs are in the log group
`/aws/lambda/${{ values.apiName }}`; API Gateway's standard metrics are in the
`AWS/ApiGateway` namespace. Set `enable_monitoring` to add access logs, alarms
and a dashboard.
{% endif %}
{%- if values.enableXRay %}
Traces of each request through API Gateway and the function are in X-Ray
(CloudWatch → Traces).
{% endif %}
## Shared modules

`infra/` uses modules of the platform's Terraform module library, pinned to a
commit of `github.com/ayoinc/cloud-sandbox-backstage`:

| Module | Used for |
| ------ | -------- |
| `aws/resources/compute/lambda` | The function{% if authType == 'jwt' %} and the authorizer{% endif %} |
| `aws/resources/core/iam-role` | Execution and logging roles |
| `aws/resources/security/waf` | Web ACL |
| `aws/resources/monitoring/cloudwatch` | Access log group, alarms, dashboard |

To take a newer version of a module, change the `ref` in its `source`.
